# PinballWizard reranker-sensitive HARD-eval golden set (v1, classified 2026-06-30).
# Companion to wizard.v2.jsonl (does NOT replace it). Same row schema (raw OPDB ids, no mch_ prefix)
# plus the hard-set fields: slice / source / first_stage_rank. See
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-30-rerank-hard-eval-design.md and ADR-0024 (Phase 4.5 H5b-hard outcome).
#
# Curated against the LIVE pinwiz-rag-v1 index (27,572 chunks / 306 machine_ids) over two waves (62 questions),
# then classified by `--probe-retrieval` (first-stage AI Search hybrid+semantic order, reranker OFF).
# slice is derived from the gold MACHINE's first-stage rank: easy = 1..TopN(5); reranker-sensitive = (5,TopK=10];
# retrieval-miss = gold machine not in the top-10 (a first-stage/embedding gap the reranker cannot fix).
#
# EMPIRICAL SLICE DISTRIBUTION (2026-06-30 probe): easy=58  reranker-sensitive=3  retrieval-miss=1.
# Finding: first-stage retrieval already resolves the correct machine into the agent's top-5 for 94% of even
# deliberately-hard, adversarially-phrased questions (49/62 at rank 1). The reranker-sensitive slice is
# structurally small on this corpus because citations are MACHINE-level and gold machines carry many chunks —
# the only reliable way to push a gold to rank 6..10 is a low-chunk gold against a theme-similar high-chunk
# distractor named as a contrastive foil (hard-adv-0021/0023/0030). This independently corroborates the v2 A/B
# null (control 0.965 ~= treatment 0.963): there is little machine-level reordering headroom for the reranker.
